## Original Content
In Spanish, both verbs mean “to be.” Here are 2 tricks for knowing when to use them!

## Summary
This article explains the difference between the Spanish verbs 'ser' and 'estar,' both of which translate to 'to be' in English. It provides two practical tricks to help learners know when to use each verb correctly.

## Key Points
- Both 'ser' and 'estar' translate to 'to be' in English but are used differently in Spanish.
- The article offers two tricks to distinguish their usage.
- Understanding the difference is key to proper Spanish grammar.


